WLD Polish GOPR Caving Expedition report  Polish GOPR (Mountain and Cave Rescue Organization) Caving Expedition took
place from 14th to 20th February in the Grigna massif by the lake Como in Lombardia, Italy. 
The aim of the expedition was to reach the bottom and explore the cave Abisso Viva le Donne -1200. 
All the participants: Pawel Kroh, Tomasz Piprek, Tomasz Krotowski, Jakub Pysz, Anna Michalek and Greg Michalek
reached -1200 on 16th February after having set a camp at -900.  The team set off at 8 am on 15th February from
Rifugio Cainallo and approached the entrance of the cave at 4 pm.  The descent from the entrance to the camp took
6 hours and from the camp to the bottom and back 5 hours.  On 16th and 17th the team explored
Freatici di Sinistra -1100 and reached the sump at the end of the passage which was non-negotiable.
Three members also explored the part called Belfangor.  The ascent from the camp to the entrance took 10 hours.  
The most difficult part of the expedition was the return from the entrance on the surface. The deteriorating weather
conditions including heavy snowfall made it long and tiring. The whole party had skis and moved extremely carefully
to avoid induced and self-induced avalanches.  The team had to change the route and went down to Cortenova.
Thanks to a local police officer, a member of the team was given a lift to Cainallo, brought the van and drove
the others back to Cainallo.  The team departed from the Refugio the following morning.
